/-!
# Integral kernels and cokernels of actual regular-family monodromy differences

The source difference operators are formed from the actual singular-homology
maps of the two geometric triangle generators. The positive period markings
conjugate them to the proved integral lattice-difference matrices.

In degrees zero through four, their literal kernels are free of respective
ranks `2, 5, 7, 5, 2`, and every literal quotient cokernel is infinite cyclic.
The cokernel equivalences in degrees one, two, and three evaluate an actual
homology representative by its marked coordinates `x 0`, `6 * x 2 + x 3`,
and `x 0`, respectively. Thus the formulas retain the actual fibre-homology
representative, including its integral normalization.

The degree-four action is proved trivial on actual top singular homology;
it is not inferred from a merely assigned determinant representation.
No conclusion about the total family's homology is assumed in this package.
-/
